        "committer": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-07 13:35:14.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20887 lfu: an OST object's owner in the Object Stream",
        "message": "LU-20887 lfu: an OST object's owner in the Object Stream\n\nAn OST object records the MDT file it belongs to: the parent\nFID in its trusted.fid, or in the LMA on an OST whose inodes\nhave no room for a second xattr (LMAC_STRIPE_INFO). A device\nscan of a stopped OST already reads it and answers\nLLAPI_SCAN_OWNER. The Object Stream of an OST in service did\nnot carry it, so a scan there could list the objects but not\nthe files they belong to.\n\nThat is the scan a drain of an OST needs. The OST stays\nmounted while its files are migrated away, and the files\nwith objects on it are found from the OST itself instead of\nfrom a scan of every MDT.\n\ndt_otable_lfu_rec() now asks DORA_XATTR for trusted.fid on\nan object whose LMA says LMAC_FID_ON_OST, or that has no LMA\nat all, and takes the parent from the LMA when\nLMAC_STRIPE_INFO says it is there. On an MDT the question is\nnot asked, except for the few objects with no LMA.\n\nThe FID goes in the record's tail, after the link, as struct\nlfu_owner, and LFU_REC_HAVE_OWNER says it is there. The\nheader keeps its size and LFU_WIRE_VERSION is not bumped: a\nreader that does not know the bit skips the bytes with\nlr_reclen, and a reader that does finds no bit from an older\nserver. That matters for the stream a client reads over\nOBD_IDX_READ, which has no size to negotiate. The tail as a\nwhole stays within LFU_LINK_MAX, so no buffer grows; an OST\nobject has no link, so the owner is all its tail holds.\n\nIn userspace scan_lfu_rec_to_obj() hands the owner to the\nscanner as the head of a trusted.fid, which is all\nscan_owner() reads of one. So the kernel backend answers\nLLAPI_SCAN_OWNER, and lfind --fid2path names the objects of\na mounted OST by their files. scan_lfu_rec_ok() refuses a\nrecord whose owner would lie outside it.\n\nAn object that was created and never written has no parent\nFID on the OST and is still reported without an owner.\n\nconf-sanity test_305 scans a mounted ldiskfs OST through\nlfu.ko and checks that every written file is named and the\nempty one is not. It skips where the module is not there.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5.5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib98c77aaab0fcafc162a733f70b403accfbd5210\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
